  "id": "Compound::DB06204 - Gene::4988",
  "verbalization": "The integrated evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Tapentadol interacts with Oprm1, the mu-opioid receptor. The visible paths indicate that Tapentadol is classified as an opioid agonist, which is consistent with its known pharmacological profile. This classification is further supported by the direct binding of Tapentadol to Oprk1, an opioid receptor, which is part of the broader opioid receptor activity pathway. The interaction between Tapentadol and Oprk1 is then linked to Oprm1, suggesting a possible mechanism of action involving the mu-opioid receptor. The lowest common ancestor of Tapentadol and Loperamide, both of which bind to Oprm1, reinforces the biological relevance of this interaction. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct involvement of Tapentadol in Oprm1 activation.",
